From 682db942d1bf4385bc149cadf1a4e120f048f1b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:42:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Ignore installer output (app/, cache/, themes/)

paths.py stores bulk data under ~/goinfre/wallpaper-studio. When the repo is cloned
to that same path, the installer writes app/ (a stale copy of the package with
absolute home paths), cache/ and themes/ (downloaded adw-gtk3) into the working tree.
Ignore them going forward. Already-tracked files need: git rm -r --cached app cache themes
---
 .gitignore | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 00f2d38..4a29093 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -1,3 +1,9 @@
 __pycache__/
 *.pyc
 .venv/
+
+# Installer output. paths.py puts bulk data in ~/goinfre/wallpaper-studio, which
+# is also where a clone usually lives, so these land inside the working tree.
+/app/
+/cache/
+/themes/
-- 
2.43.0

